+## Proposed, awaiting the steward
+
+Recorded 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment. None of these is decided; work that depends on one waits for the steward's recorded answer, which should replace the entry here. Open question Q1 (who the steward is) is in `TODO.md` "Current state".
+
+### Proposed: intent changes need the steward's recorded decision (Q2)
+
+**Context**: `INTENT.md` (header note and closing line), `AGENTS.md` ("Consult INTENT.md for significant decisions") and the local guard's check 3 each invite any contributor, human or agent, to edit `INTENT.md` when work refines or challenges it. A session can therefore change the north star to match its own work, which is the intent drift `INTENT.md` calls catastrophic to recover.
+**Proposal**: A session records a proposed intent change here, marked as awaiting the steward. `INTENT.md` changes only after the steward records the decision.
+**Depends on it**: the wording of those three places, and the Intent section of the updated local guard.
+
+### Proposed: one skill writes guards (Q3)
+
+**Context**: Two exported skills write guards with different templates: `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 (Steps 6 to 8) and `session-coherence-skill-generator`. "Specialize first around docs-first planning repos..." below backs the first; "Session-coherence generation should bootstrap young repos..." below backs the second; `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle" names only the assessment workflow. No route from `entropy-assessment` reaches `session-coherence-skill-generator`.
+**Proposal**: `session-coherence-skill-generator` becomes the only guard writer; `docs-first-planning-assessment` supplies its docs-first checks to it; `entropy-assessment` routes young repos to its bootstrap mode.
+**Depends on it**: consolidating the two skills, `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle", and the README and AGENTS.md skill descriptions.
+
+### Proposed: what the validation batch measures (Q4)
+
+**Context**: "Farm broader entropic-immunity exploration into a sibling repo" below says to assess open source projects and track whether that produces more merged PRs. `INTENT.md` "Scope boundary and next validation loop" and `README.md` "Project status" say to assess docs-first planning repos and track clearer session recovery, fewer reintroduced stale ideas, more coherent docs and sharper feedback.
+**Proposal**: Measure what `INTENT.md` lists; record merged PRs only for assessed repos that take pull requests.
+**Depends on it**: how `TODO.md` Next Up item 2 is tracked, and `README.md` "Project status".
+
